// ============================================
// Calibration Guide
// ============================================
/*
How to find your OCCUPIED_THRESHOLD:

1. Upload the code with any threshold value (e.g., 512)
2. Open Serial Monitor (Tools → Serial Monitor, 115200 baud)
3. Observe "Sensor value: XXX" when bed is EMPTY
   Example: Values around 50-150
4. Get in bed and observe values when OCCUPIED
   Example: Values around 600-800
5. Calculate threshold:
   OCCUPIED_THRESHOLD = (Empty_Average + Occupied_Average) / 2
   Example: (100 + 700) / 2 = 400
6. Update the code with your calculated threshold
7. Re-upload and test

Typical values:
- FSR Sensor: 200-600 (depends on resistance)
- Load Cell: Will need code modification for weight
- Pressure Switch: Usually digital, needs different approach
*/

